From f1c954ebb296088ccf0552f4728bfe2861f89740 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Xiwen <forbidden405@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Feb 2024 01:09:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] dt-bindings: clock: add the Hi3798MV200 CRG ids

The Hi3798MV200 is similar to the Hi3798CV200 but provides a different
set of clocks.

Number every clock field of the core CRG -- gate, source select,
divider, phase shifter and PLL -- with one id each, in ascending
(register offset, field low bit) order, generated from the register file
instead of typed. The SDIO0, SDIO1, eMMC, ComboPHY, FEMAC and GMAC
source selects take their hardware ids, while the AIAO source mux and
the two fixed VDP divider copies, which the device tree never names,
stay above the published space, and the published macro names keep their
spelling so the device tree changes no text. Publish the per-SoC id
headers for the core CRG and the system controller.

Signed-off-by: Yang Xiwen <forbidden405@outlook.com>
Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
---
 .../clock/hisilicon,hi3798mv200-crg.h         | 343 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../clock/hisilicon,hi3798mv200-sysctrl.h     |  21 ++
 2 files changed, 364 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 include/dt-bindings/clock/hisilicon,hi3798mv200-crg.h
 create mode 100644 include/dt-bindings/clock/hisilicon,hi3798mv200-sysctrl.h

--- /dev/null
